  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1}\n  [inst : MeasurableSpace E] [inst_1 : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_2 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n  [inst_3 : FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [BorelSpace E] (μ : MeasureTheory.Measure E) [MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure μ]\n  (η : NNReal × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E) → ℝ),\n  Measurable η →\n    ∀ (κ c Δ γ C : ℝ),\n      1 ≤ κ →\n        0 < c →\n          c < 1 / 4 →\n            (∀ (s : NNReal × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)), 0 < η s ∧ η s ≤ c) →\n              0 < Module.finrank ℝ E →\n                0 < Δ →\n                  Δ ≤ 1 / 2 →\n                    0 < γ →\n                      γ ≤ 1 →\n                        8 ≤ C →\n                          ∀ (s0 : NNReal × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)),\n                            have K := fun r => (1 + r) / (κ⁻¹ + r);\n                            have τ := fun r => if 2 ≤ K r then K r else c;\n                            have a := fun s => (η s + τ ↑s.1) / (1 + ↑s.1);\n                            have ell := 2 + Real.log (K ↑s0.1 * ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) * 2 / Δ);\n                            have B := γ / (√(↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) * ell) + ell);\n                            have J := ⌈C * Real.log (Real.exp 1 * K ↑s0.1 / B)⌉₊;\n                            let D := {s | B⁻¹ ≤ ↑s.1};\n                            ∃ T H,\n                              ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel T ∧\n                                ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel H ∧\n                                  (∀ (s : NNReal × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)),\n                                      T s = μ.tilted fun x => -(↑s.1 / 2) * ‖x - s.2.1‖ ^ 2) ∧\n                                    (∀ (s : NNReal × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)),\n                                        H s =\n                                          AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.GaussianSmoothing.gaussianSmoothing\n                                            (T s) √(a s)) ∧\n                                      ∀ (M L : ProbabilityTheory.Kernel (NNReal × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)) E),\n                                        ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel M →\n                                          ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel L →\n                                            (∀ s ∉ D,\n                                                AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.WassersteinSpace.wassersteinDistance\n                                                      (M s)\n                                                      (AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.GaussianSmoothing.gaussianSmoothing\n                                                        (T s) √(η s / (1 + ↑s.1))) ^\n                                                    2 ≤\n                                                  ENNReal.ofReal\n                                                    (K ↑s.1 * (2 * τ ↑s.1 * Δ ^ 2 / (K ↑s.1 * (↑J + 1))) /\n                                                      (1 + ↑s.1))) →\n                                              ∃ F Q P R,\n                                                (∀ (s : NNReal × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)) (y : E),\n                                                    ↑(F (s, y)).1 = ↑s.1 + (a s)⁻¹ ∧\n                                                      (F (s, y)).2 =\n                                                        ((↑s.1 + (a s)⁻¹)⁻¹ • (↑s.1 • s.2.1 + (a s)⁻¹ • y), s.2.2.1 + 1,\n                                                          fun n => Nat.casesOn n y s.2.2.2)) ∧\n                                                  ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel Q ∧\n                                                    ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel P ∧\n                                                      (∀ (n : ℕ), ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel (R n)) ∧\n                                                        (∀ (s : NNReal × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)),\n                                                            Q s =\n                                                              AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.GaussianSmoothing.gaussianSmoothing\n                                                                (M s) √(τ ↑s.1 / (1 + ↑s.1))) ∧\n                                                          (∀ (s : NNReal × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)),\n                                                              P s =\n                                                                if s ∈ D then MeasureTheory.Measure.dirac s\n                                                                else\n                                                                  MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun y => F (s, y)) (Q s)) ∧\n                                                            (∀ (n : ℕ), R n = L.comp (P ^ n)) ∧\n                                                              0 < B ∧\n                                                                ((P ^ J) s0) D = 1 ∧\n                                                                  (∀ (m : ℕ), (R (J + m)) s0 = (R J) s0) ∧\n                                                                    InformationTheory.klDiv ((R J) s0) (T s0) ≤\n                                                                        ↑J * ENNReal.ofReal (Δ ^ 2 / (↑J + 1)) +\n                                                                          ∫⁻ (x : NNReal × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)) in D,\n                                                                            InformationTheory.klDiv (L x)\n                                                                              (T x) ∂(P ^ J) s0 ∧\n                                                                      ((∀ s ∈ D,\n                                                                          InformationTheory.klDiv (L s) (T s) ≤\n                                                                            ENNReal.ofReal (Δ ^ 2 / (↑J + 1))) →\n                                                                        ∀ (m : ℕ),\n                                                                          InformationTheory.klDiv ((R (J + m)) s0)\n                                                                              (T s0) ≤\n                                                                            ENNReal.ofReal (Δ ^ 2))",
    "statement_sha256": "ad8dbf2d012d285953c65bcd8e51f1011b5bc54944865ea10d77da83f9b515ef",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "Measure E is a countably additive measure, IsProbabilityMeasure means mass one. A Markov kernel is a measurable family of probability measures.",
      "State is NNReal times E times Nat times (Nat to E). For s=(b,u,k,h), s.1=b and s.2=(u,k,h). Nat.casesOn n y h prepends y to history. Vector products are scalar multiplication.",
      "Measure.tilted mu f normalizes exp(f) against mu. GaussianSmoothing.gaussianSmoothing nu sigma adds independent centered isotropic Gaussian noise of standard deviation sigma, so its covariance is sigma squared times identity.",
      "WassersteinSpace.wassersteinDistance is the actual extended-nonnegative quadratic transport distance used here; its square equals the infimum quadratic displacement cost over couplings. A finite cross displacement bound alone does not assert marginal second moments. klDiv is extended-nonnegative relative entropy.",
      "Measure.map is pushforward, bind integrates a measure-valued function, and dirac is point mass. P^n is n successive transitions, P^0 identity. Nonnegative integrals can be infinite. n in the displayed multiplication is cast to ENNReal, J in the accuracy expression is cast to Real.",
      "Set restriction of a measure to D retains only mass on D. A displayed integral over D is a nonnegative integral against that restricted measure. Nat.ceil maps a real number to its nonnegative integer ceiling. The state coordinate b is coerced from NNReal to Real in scalar formulas."
    ]
  },
